18.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key competing hypotheses after round 0: (1) Semiramide (Alboni title role 1843 Scala revival; Caruso sang Idreno ~1918 Met; 1990 Met return after >70-yr gap; Assur by Samuel Ramey—supported by cols 1,13,16,17); (2) La Cenerentola (Alboni 1843; Caruso as Ramiro ~1910s; 1997 Met revival; bass role Alidoro/Don Magnifico variously Ramey, Alaimo, or Dara—cols 4,11,12,15,18); (3) La Favorita (Alboni as Leonora 1843; Caruso as Fernando 1905; 1978 OONY/Met revival; Baldassare by Giaiotti or Siepi—cols 3,5,6,8,20). 

Disagreements center on which work Alboni actually headlined in 1843 Scala, exact Caruso role/timeline, and whether “first time…staged in NYC” means literal premiere or first post-gap revival. Errors noted: several mis-assign Caruso to bass parts (e.g., Assur) or wrong revival dates. Strongest convergence on Semiramide + Ramey given documented Met history and multiple independent matches. Unresolved: precise 1843 Scala bill and whether any production was truly “first in NYC.” 

Current lean: Semiramide, Samuel Ramey as Assur.}

